ving to othe religions but DO NOT SAY THAT ITS CHRISTIANITIES RIGHT TO CONVERT.THIS IS NOT GURANTEED UNDER THE CONSTITUTION,NEITHER DOES IT SAY ITS OK TO CONV'),(7963,'http://www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=de847806-8ec0-4ed2-aff5-e9317f5539d3&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+the+real+Hindu?&strParent=strParentID','guest5371','2008-08-30 12:48:25','ERT PEOPLE'),(7964,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=2aba4a87-93bc-439c-b6a2-cc560e8ad12a&&Headline=I+havent+been+home+in+three+years:+Deepika&strParent=strParentID','guest4104','2008-08-30 12:51:17','wow, the proce you pay for being a film star'),(7965,'http://www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=de847806-8ec0-4ed2-aff5-e9317f5539d3&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+the+real+Hindu?&strParent=strParentID','guest4104','2008-08-30 12:54:33','hi'),(7966,'http://www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=de847806-8ec0-4ed2-aff5-e9317f5539d3&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+the+real+Hindu?&strParent=strParentID','guest5730','2008-08-30 13:42:27','Karan Thapar: â€œLet me put it bluntly, even crudely. If I want to sell my soul â€” and trade in my present gods for a new lot â€” why shouldnâ€™t I? Even if the act diminishes me in your eyes, itâ€™s my right to do so.â€\r\n\r\nDear Karan,\r\nTo put your argument in proper perspective, please replace the word â€œsoulâ€ with â€œdaughterâ€ or â€œbrotherâ€ or â€œown personâ€. Then, you become a â€œsex workerâ€ or â€œpimpâ€ depending on what you are â€œtradingâ€ in, the person inducing you to such a trade becomes a â€œpimpâ€ or a â€œcustomerâ€ and the entire â€œtradeâ€ becomes illegal. \r\n\r\nBut, this is not the point here. What is missed in the entire debate is the intolerance within a few religions to establish their superiority vis-a-vis other religions, that they are not content until the entire world follows their faith. Herein lies the crux of the problem of global terrorism, which may result in the inevitable clash of the religions in not too distant future.\r\nWith best wishes\r\nGuest'),(7967,'http://www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=de847806-8ec0-4ed2-aff5-e9317f5539d3&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+the+real+Hindu?&strParent=strParentID','guest4565','2008-08-30 15:13:41','Congrats Karan Thapar, for your boldness & honesty. I wish this will open the eyes of our religious and national leaders. Please arrange it to be translated and publish in Oriya news papers too.'),(7968,'http://www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=de847806-8ec0-4ed2-aff5-e9317f5539d3&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+the+real+Hindu?&strParent=strParentID','guest4565','2008-08-30 15:17:48','For generations, we grew up in Kerala surrounded by Hindus, Christians, Muslims, and other low castes. We shares in the joys and sorrows of each other family.  When calamities like flood occur, we cuddle up under one shelter and eat from the same plate.  Us and our children grew up together studying, competing, still keeping our individual faith, without any conflict.  Even in matters of job opportunities abroad, we help each other.  This is called real brotherhood; this is what Gandhiji and other saints of various religions taught us.'),(7969,'http://www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=de847806-8ec0-4ed2-aff5-e9317f5539d3&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+the+real+Hindu?&strParent=strParentID','guest4565','2008-08-30 15:18:52','In no way the present carnage in Orissa is justified by humans, or in the eyes of God.'),(7970,'http://www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=de847806-8ec0-4ed2-aff5-e9317f5539d3&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+the+real+Hindu?&strParent=strParentID','guest4565','2008-08-30 15:20:12','Whoever killed the Swami must be identified and brought to justice; and whoever is behind this present carnage must be brought to light and dealt with according to the law.'),(7971,'http://www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=de847806-8ec0-4ed2-aff5-e9317f5539d3&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+the+real+Hindu?&strParent=strParentID','guest4565','2008-08-30 15:23:37','The constitution of India gives every citizen the right to preach, practice, and promote his faith.  No one can stop another person from accepting another religion.  History will show Christians converting to Hinduism, Islam and other religions; and vice versa, Muslims to Hinduism; Hindus to Muslim; and Hindus to Christianity - even to Atheism.'),(7972,'http://www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=de847806-8ec0-4ed2-aff5-e9317f5539d3&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+the+real+Hindu?&strParent=strParentID','guest4565','2008-08-30 15:25:11','That is no reason for murder and destruction of an entire religion in Orissa.  This is worse than carnal. One day they will be accountable to God for all this.'),(7973,'http://www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=de847806-8ec0-4ed2-aff5-e9317f5539d3&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+the+real+Hindu?&strParent=strParentID','guest4565','2008-08-30 15:25:23','JVT'),(7974,'dogtimemedia.com','guest2804','2008-08-30 16:33:22','hello'),(7975,'http://www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=de847806-8ec0-4ed2-aff5-e9317f5539d3&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+the+real+Hindu?&strParent=strParentID','guest6534','2008-08-30 17:11:07','Most countries and religions do not allow converting to other religions. Also, with conversions, the landscape and culture will change. And finally, other reloiions do not have the same caste system as Hindus. So, why have reservations after conversion to outside of hinduism? Violence is not the answer to these issues. However, conversion to other religions need a policical debate and need to be understood in the context of long term consequences as well.'),(7976,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=47198453-7312-4fa6-a237-ac1fe76bbe71&&Headline=Goodbye+Musharraf&strParent=strParentID','guest3277','2008-08-30 18:03:40','this has to stop'),(7977,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=47198453-7312-4fa6-a237-ac1fe76bbe71&&Headline=Goodbye+Musharraf&strParent=strParentID','guest3277','2008-08-30 18:03:51','obama and his camp are openly saying'),(7978,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=47198453-7312-4fa6-a237-ac1fe76bbe71&&Headline=Goodbye+Musharraf&strParent=strParentID','guest3277','2008-08-30 18:04:06','that they have to stop terrorists in iraq, afghanistan'),(7979,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=47198453-7312-4fa6-a237-ac1fe76bbe71&&Headline=Goodbye+Musharraf&strParent=strParentID','guest3277','2008-08-30 18:04:10','and pakistan'),(7980,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?id=de935467-3311-4e4c-b4d5-d83519c8aa00&ParentID=9d8e9189-2bd2-4e89-a13d-b94256c02d5a&&Headline=Singur:+Many+questions,+many+answers..','guest3277','2008-08-30 18:04:49','great covrerage'),(7981,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/FullcoverageStoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=b0b254bd-35fe-4726-83f8-ae5834062444HTpaystributestoDrKKBirla_Special&&Headline=End+of+an+era','guest3277','2008-08-30 18:05:10','birla empire is not the same'),(7982,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/FullcoverageStoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=b0b254bd-35fe-4726-83f8-ae5834062444HTpaystributestoDrKKBirla_Special&&Headline=End+of+an+era','guest3277','2008-08-30 18:05:17','it used to be tata\\\'s and birlas'),(7983,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/FullcoverageStoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=b0b254bd-35fe-4726-83f8-ae5834062444HTpaystributestoDrKKBirla_Special&&Headline=End+of+an+era','guest3277','2008-08-30 18:05:34','I guess, now its a