 land (bigger size) & farm from the money they get. No body will Invest in India, when capital costs itself (such as land) are too expensive. Industries create lots of employment. A Tata plant employing 10,000 people in its plant provides indirect employment for another 1,00,000. You want to see examples. Detroit? A whole city is dependent on Automobile plants!!!! Reporters, newspapers please be responsible.'),(10229,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8594','2008-10-05 22:30:21','crying as I wright this. my dog keeps peeing in my bed right where I sleep. what does it mean'),(10230,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8594','2008-10-05 22:30:42','write'),(10231,'www.hulu.com','guest8763','2008-10-05 22:53:12','HI'),(10232,'www.hulu.com','guest8763','2008-10-05 22:53:22','COOL'),(10233,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=25c3d8e9-74e5-43e8-94d3-dd1d2be21992&&Headline=Whose+brakes+failed?','guest9690','2008-10-06 03:18:18','Its a good counter artical.e Till now Tata\\\'s have been made the sufferer and Trinamool the tormentor. but this article puts the points in perspective. I guess Tata is also like any other businessman. Noone has time to think about poor.'),(10234,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=25c3d8e9-74e5-43e8-94d3-dd1d2be21992&&Headline=Whose+brakes+failed?','guest8370','2008-10-06 04:58:31','If buying land was so easy then West Bengal government could have compensated land for land but that is not possible and someone in Detroit may not realise the ground realities in Bengal--all in all it is better that Buddha got out of this mess as the future would have brought more misery and this would have haunted him to his death'),(10235,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=25c3d8e9-74e5-43e8-94d3-dd1d2be21992&&Headline=Whose+brakes+failed?','guest2961','2008-10-06 05:27:01','But what he has proved, beyond a shadow of doubt, is that he is no Jamshed Tata.\r\n-------- >'),(10236,